If you bribe them, they ALSO aren't there on the way up.

And in at least part, he's talking about a real-time saving factor.
Something that isn't often taken into consideration is that Nethack is
actually a fairly long game, where even 'skilled' ascenders have to
really work to reduce a game to under 6 hours of play.

If you're playing in, say, devnull or the June NAO tourney, then real
time becomes even more important as you only have 30 days available, not
all of which you'll be able to devote to gaming.  

If you're trying for the major trophies, you simply can't spend 3-4 days
on each game leisurely exploring; you are going to need to know how to ascend
consistently and efficiently.  It's far more deleterious to your efforts to die
in Gehennom to a fluke circumstance than it is to die on DL3 to a wand of
striking after 10 minutes of play; as such, this is one of the tricks that 
has evolved.  Bribed demons don't interact with you hostilely, and
_don't_ summon other demons, etc. -- it's a 100% effective means of
removing the demon at no risk to yourself.

